#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/agents-context-management.rst:7
msgid ""
"Mattermost Agents are designed to handle context efficiently, ensuring "
"that only necessary information is sent to the Large Language Model (LLM)"
" for generating accurate responses. This document outlines how Agents "
"process and include relevant context. The company name, the server name, "
"and the time are always passed to the LLM to ensure accurate and "
"contextually relevant responses."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/agents-context-management.rst:10
msgid "**Ensure data privacy**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/end-user-guide/collaborate/agents-context-management.rst:12
msgid ""
"We recommend that customers with strict privacy requirements run the LLM "
"locally to prevent sensitive data, including personally identifiable "
"information (PII) and message content, from being shared with an external"
" LLM hosting vendor. This ensures data privacy while enabling Agent "
"functionality."
msgstr ""

